ai-digest Repository Version History
====================================

v1.2.3 (Release Date: TBD)
--------------------------
- Split plain-mode Japanese summaries after Japanese sentence terminators even
  when no whitespace follows.
- Require the sole build_report tool on the OpenAI-compatible backend without
  using a named function choice, allowing thinking models such as Kimi K3.
- Require an explicit SUMMARIZER_BASE_URL for the openai-compatible backend,
  failing early when it is missing or blank.
- Build a report in a staging directory and publish it whole only once complete,
  so a failed run can no longer leave a half-written report.
- Reject invalid numeric settings instead of silently using defaults or failing
  later in a run.
- Scope configuration to each command and the viewer so unrelated settings cannot
  stop independent paths.
- Reject impossible calendar dates before report work begins or archive paths are
  accepted.
- Reject unusable explicit font paths instead of silently selecting another font.
- Require HTTPS for source collection and image scraping, refusing downgrade
  redirects before any plaintext request is sent.

v1.2.2 (2026-08-26)
-------------------
- Add doc/REQUIREMENTS.md and doc/BASIC_DESIGN.md, separating what the system is
  required to do from how it is built, and reference both from README.
- Treat structurally invalid report files as corrupt instead of crashing, and
  reject a stored date that doesn't match its report directory.
- Complete the versioning rules in doc/POLICY.md.
- Make the summary-image attribution backend-neutral so plain reports are not
  labeled as AI-generated.

v1.2.1 (2026-08-09)
-------------------
- Add .gitattributes, marking the Markdown documents for diff.
- Rename doc/POLICY and doc/LICENSE to doc/POLICY.md and doc/LICENSE.md, so that
  GitHub renders them, and update the references to them.
- Expand doc/POLICY.md into a standalone policy covering environment differences,
  repeated execution, naming, and pull request scope.
- Summarize the entries of this file to one bullet per change, as doc/POLICY.md
  has always asked.
- Add the shared version history description guidelines to the end of this file.

v1.2 (2026-08-05)
-----------------
- Rename the endpoint settings from ANTHROPIC_*/OPENAI_* to a single SUMMARIZER_*
  set naming the wire protocol; CLI options follow suit.
- Refuse the superseded setting names at startup. Upgrading a host means unsetting
  them wherever they were exported, not only editing .env.
- Bound the summarization request with SUMMARIZER_TIMEOUT, defaulting to 180
  seconds, so that HTTP_TIMEOUT now covers only the collectors and the scraper.
- Raise MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS's default to 8000, HTTP_TIMEOUT's to 60 seconds, and
  move the viewer from port 5000 to 3000.
- Document USER_AGENT in .env.example.
- Add doc/DEPLOYMENT.md and deploy/, covering the Debian and nginx procedure and
  the routine operations.
- Describe the exit codes, the failure log lines and how to add a collector in the
  README.
- List doc/POLICY and doc/VERSIONS in the repository structure and link them from
  the top of the README.

v1.1.1 (2026-08-04)
-------------------
- Read the feed timestamps as UTC, which is what feedparser returns; a host east
  of UTC had been losing the offset from its look back window.
- Name the configured look back window in the prompt and in the summary image
  instead of always announcing 24 hours.
- Report why a run collected nothing: unreachable sources, nothing published in
  the window, or none configured; partial loss still continues.
- Copy the composite image of the captured report into doc/screenshots from
  tools/capture_screens.py.
- Accept every setting as a cli.py option named after its variable; the three
  credentials have none, since a command line is world-readable.
- Keep the categories of the leading topics in the legend of the summary image.
- Draw a card instead of ending the run when an image is refused as a
  decompression bomb.
- Record the look-back window a run collected in its report's statistics, so
  'cli.py render' redraws with the period it was built from.
- Fall back on the default identity when USER_AGENT is set but empty.
- Apply the line limit of wrap_text() to an explicit line break as well.

v1.1 (2026-08-02)
-----------------
- Stop the batch on an unknown SUMMARIZER_BACKEND value instead of falling back on
  the default, and remove the unused Config.require_api_key().
- Accept only http and https links from the collectors, and neutralize the ones
  already stored when a report is rendered.
- Enforce the image size limit while reading the response, not after buffering the
  whole body, and request images over http/https only.
- Anchor the report date pattern with \A and \Z.
- Cover the configuration, the report paths, the link filtering, the capped
  download and the plain backend with unit tests.
- Add ANTHROPIC_THINKING_MODE and ANTHROPIC_TOOL_CHOICE_MODE (accepting 'any') for
  endpoints that never return a tool_use block by default.
- Add ANTHROPIC_TEXT_JSON_FALLBACK, off by default, which reads a report an
  endpoint wrote as JSON text rather than as a tool call.
- Read MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS from the environment, where it had been a constant in the
  summarizer.
- Add ANTHROPIC_MAX_RETRIES.
- Add SUMMARIZER_BACKEND=openai, an OpenAI-compatible path validated through the
  same to_topics(); the openai package is imported only when used.
- Name the stop reason and block types when no build_report call is found, accept
  only a block named build_report, and log one summary line per response.
- Add doc/POLICY, the ai-digest implementation policy adapted for a single Python
  project from the shared id774/scripts policy.

v1.0 (2026-07-31)
-----------------
- Add the 'demo' command, building a report from the bundled sample without
  calling the API, documented with screenshots from tools/capture_screens.py.
- Add SUMMARIZER_BACKEND=plain, letting the batch pipeline run without an API key
  by building topics mechanically.
- Support custom Anthropic-compatible API URLs and Bearer authentication.

v0.1 (2026-07-26)
-----------------
- Initial release.

Version History Guidelines
==========================
- Write one coherent change per bullet, at most two physical lines.
- A single line at or under 80 columns is preferred whenever practical.
  Necessary file names, command names, option names, and configuration
  names may pass 80 columns on the bullet's one or two lines when they
  cannot be shortened without losing meaning.
- When a version history already exists, balance a new entry against the
  length of the existing lines, so that the whole file stays consistent.
  Holding to the form this file has settled on comes before the two-line,
  80-column limit above, and leaves that limit standing wherever no such
  form exists.
- When an entry becomes substantially longer, omit or abstract implementation
  details, examples, reasons, and secondary effects where possible.
- Preserve the changed target, externally observable behavior, compatibility
  or security impact, and important option or configuration names.
- Combine related changes within the same version, especially changes to the
  same file or feature.
- Place closely related entries near each other.
- Append an independent new change to the end of the current version entry.
- The first entry, at the lowest version this file reaches, reads only
  "Initial release." and nothing else.
